SUMMARY:Praying for Peace & Practicing Nonviolence on World Labyrinth Day
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 2 | 9:00 AM – 2:00 PM\nIn the morning\, Father David and others will reflect on what Gandhi’s insights can teach us about nonviolent social change and the spiritual practices that have made them possible over the last century. A live practice session will give participants the opportunity to explore the dynamics and challenges of maintaining a loving and nonviolent Christian witness when encountering threats of abuse or violence. \nThe afternoon session celebrates World Labyrinth Day with a chance to deepen your personal prayers for peace by walking a labyrinth with others. Every year on the first Saturday in May\, thousands of people around the globe participate in World Labyrinth Day as a moving meditation for world peace and a celebration of the labyrinth experience. Many “Walk as One at 1:00 PM” local time to create a rolling wave of peaceful energy passing from one time zone to the next. \nRegistration required for planning purposes. This is a FREE and ACCESSIBLE event. \nSchedule\n8:30 AM – Registration and check-in\n9:00 AM – Morning session with Fr. David in the main church \n11:30 – 12:30 PM – Lunch\, bring a bag lunch or enjoy the downtown eateries \n12:30 – 2:00 PM – Labyrinth walk in the Parish House (This is an ADA accessible activity) \nPlease use the form below to let us know you’ll be joining us. \n    First name*    Last name*    Address*                                Street Address                                City                                State                            Zip Code    Phone*    Email *    How many will be in your party?*    Which sessions do you plan to attend?*MorningAfternoonBoth    How did you hear about this event? Please check all that apply.*Headlines & HappeningsSaint James websiteUrban Well eblastFrom a friendPosterFacebookFrom an event sponsorOtherRegister for this eventReset form
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/urban-well-retreat/
LOCATION:Saint James Episcopal Church\, 103 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Urban-Well-Retreat-FEATURED-IMAGE-copy.jpg
GEO:40.040058;-76.30344
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Saint James Episcopal Church 103 North Duke Street Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=103 North Duke Street:geo:-76.30344,40.040058
END:VEVENT
